  "notes": [
   "Buzzer legs are read from the circuit image as column 5 and column 8, row h of the breadboard half with rows f-j (bank 'b').",
   "Buzzer port 1 is taken as the positive (+) leg and port 2 as the negative (-) leg. The schematic connects + to pin 8 and - to GND, so the column-8 leg is + and the column-5 leg is -.",
   "The black wire goes to the GND pin next to AREF, near pin 13. I mapped it to GND.1 because the catalogue doesn't say which GND header pin that is.",
   "Wires are placed in row f of columns 5 and 8, the same column strips as the buzzer legs.",
   "The manual says 'piezo buzzer or a speaker'. I used the piezo buzzer, as the circuit image does.",
   "Software (the melody sketch and pitches.h) isn't part of the physical graph."
  ]
